{"objects":[{"id":"flow","instance":"instance--b96dad5f-c519-5a1f-a718-912ca4a86c02","objects":["attack-action--1","attack-action--2","attack-action--3","attack-action--4","attack-action--5","attack-action--6","attack-action--7","attack-action--8","attack-action--9","attack-action--10","attack-action--11","attack-action--12","attack-action--13","attack-action--14","attack-action--15","attack-action--16","attack-action--17","attack-action--18","attack-action--19","attack-action--20","attack-action--21","attack-action--22","attack-condition--1","attack-condition--2","attack-condition--3","file--replicator-applescript","instance--bc9da4c9-c99e-5da4-97fe-e3ffbcaed42c","file--pods","file--cat","instance--100b57e0-803f-5bff-b564-7d8a76b25a63","instance--ed1c0e58-b882-535b-b531-2e1bd7b22964","process--codesign","instance--d8125ab2-3041-549b-ba8b-7afd80c5b756","instance--5d35516b-4240-50c3-8646-4592780adbea","domain-name--trendmicronano","ipv4-addr--94-130-27-189","instance--6f46e055-ae20-51b9-b75a-61940162efb5","file--bootstrap-applescript","instance--b58e806f-2a40-5e3f-b452-8a3ca9127ae1","file--applekit","instance--e881b6f1-1e6e-5a4d-91b1-d31a3ae50227","instance--3536a568-610f-5570-bba9-6dfe97bc9c2e","instance--384798bd-a84b-5feb-8d38-7f9d0a087f11","instance--ed6039fe-678b-5ae9-9576-73e6ea35b0c8","instance--7e8c9301-c3f8-55e9-8894-e81f1b6203d9","instance--b6d82c28-0a68-5c6f-b058-c1e072f51852","instance--3622ace1-abf1-5f6e-a5de-a6f584dc1f66","instance--56b40d44-cc57-5e8b-b320-779a685089fd","instance--895aab9a-87c3-51d8-91f8-cc3f6dd1a5a5","instance--3bb881aa-a5ab-51ba-b53d-89d26964ce7d","instance--be99ba49-e121-58a8-ba7b-dd3de316cfcf","instance--57bd700a-faa2-5f72-95f2-2694bcea17c9","instance--4284b2d1-cb3e-5edd-9f83-66e52b005ee7","instance--71ca6229-618c-5bbf-8066-f361ecd9c8e7","instance--3e0f78a3-bb54-55bd-8490-3453d5e06d04","instance--a37796a0-93b2-51bb-be4b-2a9a9e7e35e1","instance--cb7da505-6791-507a-9a93-f9914c292d1b","instance--f9e616ac-2310-573d-8995-336b82cf51af","instance--77414a6f-10f0-5dbb-b428-351706ad11fd","instance--f9c9b265-fc34-5120-8a3d-f9bd8fbf0c0f","instance--92ee8792-942a-5a8c-9c2e-9bc59b33f65a","instance--d10e3bf2-a50f-5852-a99e-152c31cdbbe9","instance--7f599411-7d6c-5329-8ffd-634658e76c31","instance--da949e34-395e-51a5-b539-9146b39afe0f","instance--0dfc5eeb-3b64-51bb-a90a-7dc67b331b1c","instance--406ec750-1237-5c0f-8510-432397ff9d09","instance--8531e84d-c1ce-5084-8bf4-bb1a564db757","instance--1ded3586-5202-54e5-a1bc-20b18bf94669","instance--022afd20-ea74-5796-be81-65e421f33ec9","instance--778668d0-88b6-53a4-ae62-e7db9a5a13a7","instance--ec4be4b8-976a-57fa-8648-df4e49e2ace0","instance--80b71fce-2255-5f5a-8949-fa33d98ef422","instance--54e1a2a7-74cc-5291-8503-a1b7154b63a5","instance--44cfeaea-1fab-55ef-a083-59c69db10e22","instance--27444ab5-b365-5bb4-9f7d-6b907fe977c3","instance--336f6a3f-544f-5522-99df-ca8d60644c16","instance--a2d55835-86ab-50db-b442-91f1a6475118","instance--60d1d0eb-88a1-557b-bb51-d53e308370ab","instance--c150241a-dd10-516e-b59a-52ab5e530205","instance--abab6ceb-3841-59a9-aee7-d5036bf269aa","instance--15a4aa01-1509-5f1d-9fd7-27c6d953ab8d"],"properties":[["name","XCSSET adapts to macOS 11 and M1-based Macs"],["description","Trend Micro research describing XCSSET behavior on macOS 11 and M1-based Macs."],["scope","campaign"],["author",[["name","Steven Du"]]],["external_references",[["item-1",[["source_name","www.trendmicro.com"],["url","https://www.trendmicro.com/en_us/research/21/d/xcsset-quickly-adapts-to-macos-11-and-m1-based-macs.html"]]]]]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--ad592d05-6969-5b51-98a8-1ad9b6aab896","120":"instance--5850a8f4-8241-5e73-9bf0-dcd376cd5025","150":"instance--0da1498f-3beb-5916-a249-e0410a4a81e4","180":"instance--d3632784-7391-5a29-83e2-edab51db56c6","210":"instance--8bc47ca5-ca73-5a04-a9ea-918608f10871","240":"instance--6546eef6-c5ad-516e-a417-89916e651648","270":"instance--244e5a69-f465-564e-9d2c-93d4da44fc57","30":"instance--6a1fca3c-fdb6-536a-bbea-61ac2349a700","300":"instance--043a5b44-2864-5565-abce-1909204e5485","330":"instance--e10eb918-2b0b-56f4-9c82-f345ce21276c","60":"instance--33a99d1b-dad8-51f6-be74-e1614db9151b","90":"instance--380c79e9-b1eb-547c-bf01-a011db1201c1"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--1","properties":[["name","Infect Xcode projects"],["description","The replicator.applescript module infects Xcode developer projects by inserting a function that calls its malicious components during the build phase or the build rule."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0002","technique":"T1059.002"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--4f4d03a8-4502-5010-997b-9943e254395b","120":"instance--cefe62ac-5b6e-5ead-84fc-b4c632913a73","150":"instance--4d07a740-2467-5b95-ac8d-4a2ee8edd11e","180":"instance--1205f03c-a457-5a0b-87ef-3bbb7aac110f","210":"instance--96e7dc6a-9f86-5f69-8d45-a566303cd4c0","240":"instance--66237af6-bb19-5a51-9fa2-cbc4a96186f5","270":"instance--836dfd42-b475-50ca-9acf-4f11bd32b89f","30":"instance--efe92997-cc5c-538a-90bc-c09ffb1379f4","300":"instance--9c4a24ae-1426-5cb5-9d7c-792e6dd325b7","330":"instance--06c6a74a-ca7d-5703-88ea-a06a0933d21a","60":"instance--5e4f84e5-56b7-5b8f-9bc3-b4d59d371123","90":"instance--019deb6a-bab3-57db-9a53-11e3564bf7a4"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--2","properties":[["name","Insert randomized infection IDs"],["description","In previous versions, these code snippets inserted in the build phase or build rule were assigned hard-coded IDs, but this latest iteration added a new function that automatically generates random IDs. According to its logic (Figure 13), this random ID will always end with the postfix \u201cAAC43A,\u201d which is used to identify and remove the old infection snippet in preparation for a new infection (Figure 14)."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1027.010"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0ce35aea-35a2-52ae-a67b-985306bdefe7","120":"instance--312639d5-e6d9-57b1-850d-28f0a1eac2f6","150":"instance--9551a25e-2558-512e-9894-dd64a8d662bf","180":"instance--403becce-e0ad-5dcd-bc14-7c00453907da","210":"instance--2305f501-2712-5ec6-9d4e-1371b011e937","240":"instance--cf1b8cf6-1cbd-5afb-b653-aa693889dab5","270":"instance--1d3dc59a-40a0-5670-aa3e-1304ff762003","30":"instance--77063d4f-503a-5e9b-b622-15aa2cc6a8e7","300":"instance--beaab67f-8a54-5982-8c5d-9d2ed2d42c9f","330":"instance--4d3274ff-ef14-5a53-99be-01575194a98e","60":"instance--4154a6bf-290b-5fce-a557-5dc0f3e700fb","90":"instance--2992bc0b-df57-54e5-a17b-03a964338c09"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--3","properties":[["name","Call cat binary from build phase"],["description","Originally, the inserted script during the build phase or build rule calls a bash script file, which refers to Mach-O binary files as \u201cPods\u201d (Figure 15). However, in this latest version, the script calls a Mach-O binary file \u201ccat\u201d directly and is assigned the value of the AUTO_CLEAN_PROJ variable, which is currently set to \u201cfalse\u201d (Figure 16)."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0002","technique":"T1059.004"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0f6e4da7-a5f4-54d7-866f-3bc6e8bcb019","120":"instance--015254b5-0906-577e-b3e3-3899f837d118","150":"instance--f7af5b8c-330a-58d5-b0da-a3d5f0bc6ad0","180":"instance--9f27ab21-2382-567d-b022-74ad5a29bd08","210":"instance--d799eb0a-7600-5b1a-a298-c47a78ceae4b","240":"instance--911c2c52-5974-5e08-b0b6-a9084d57c6ee","270":"instance--286444b4-97a1-58cd-9ca3-cffa04a15351","30":"instance--92192c38-5143-50e0-8c39-a96ea86e32e2","300":"instance--82bb3de0-bea5-5651-a1de-583283258c6d","330":"instance--4f0945c8-f644-50ce-8796-fea52a29dda1","60":"instance--16c43a2d-7356-521d-a507-5922e2c3337b","90":"instance--abce5c62-339a-5ed5-a0b8-dd66136cfe2f"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--4","properties":[["name","Download Safari update packages"],["description","As mentioned in our first technical brief, this malware leverages the development version of Safari to load malicious Safari frameworks and related JavaScript backdoors from its C&C server. It hosts Safari update packages in the C&C server, then downloads and installs packages for the user\u2019s OS version. To adapt to the newly-released Big Sur, new packages for \u201cSafari 14\u201d were added (Figure 1). As we\u2019ve observed in , it downloads a corresponding Safari package according to the user\u2019s current browser and OS versions (Figure 2)."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1105"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--a469636c-0cb2-50b9-92f9-644c8aa98197","120":"instance--d57b3a21-e910-5879-8148-40165cea451a","150":"instance--58250ef4-5bb4-5bf3-b33e-89493bbb395d","180":"instance--3e769cf2-c1e5-5d2e-81d4-892f48ce4d86","210":"instance--f6499e41-749c-5d7f-9346-96c08d0d5dfd","240":"instance--d9dcdfc8-5f42-546a-803a-0efcd5d4cf91","270":"instance--c9afd0f6-97ce-57b2-9d60-3557b6214809","30":"instance--75f82155-f5ff-5619-8bf8-aae22937cab0","300":"instance--25e2d26e-1b35-56bd-b9aa-096c2d3b0e3c","330":"instance--e0483688-da10-5376-8cf2-050bcc3b70f0","60":"instance--1293d9cc-16b2-5c67-a453-bd144aab133a","90":"instance--2b43cd52-10db-5b15-8ad5-c4b59496528b"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--5","properties":[["name","Install malicious Safari components"],["description","As mentioned in our first technical brief, this malware leverages the development version of Safari to load malicious Safari frameworks and related JavaScript backdoors from its C&C server. It hosts Safari update packages in the C&C server, then downloads and installs packages for the user\u2019s OS version."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0003","technique":"T1574.006"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--54fc1f38-f4e3-523e-b07c-73889b0d8df7","120":"instance--9cf45948-7040-5d7a-a1d5-3cb4db0c1af6","150":"instance--13bb13cc-e02b-51d2-8d7d-40e5613b6e5a","180":"instance--e33bc6ee-771e-54fe-a772-74dfdaad420d","210":"instance--286f51a3-8fc6-55ec-978e-8b05ebda3655","240":"instance--14659696-be77-5460-beb1-4b5eac126e43","270":"instance--f48ed1a6-2895-5cd2-9b1c-e30ac2bc8921","30":"instance--7b803e61-16ac-5720-92cd-8f2a456a52b7","300":"instance--76c24361-5143-5c43-8e4d-707c619e6038","330":"instance--f395cfc7-395a-5001-9552-a4fec6dbc53a","60":"instance--760885bb-9294-5a5b-93a2-a410e1ea4112","90":"instance--8e0d1a12-8611-598d-9a7d-40f2525e4781"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--6","properties":[["name","Download icon files for imitation apps"],["description","Imitation apps for Big Sur are also created from malicious AppleScript files, in which icon files are downloaded from a C&C server, then their files are modified so that the fake app's icon is convincingly disguised as that of the legitimate app it's trying to imitate."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1105"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--7cccbcd0-a724-54fb-be4f-ac523d26f7d0","120":"instance--738e44b2-1357-5eb3-82bd-8a0ce8942b72","150":"instance--d31f4735-6339-5929-8d7c-d30863cf166f","180":"instance--2252393d-d801-5931-ad38-4b53374a9880","210":"instance--065b5ad5-023a-5336-b458-e9c9dcda2976","240":"instance--5ea0dd2b-5eac-51f8-855a-4cbcb801bc2d","270":"instance--bba66874-a069-56c6-bb95-967cb3cefc9e","30":"instance--6377c09d-ecb4-5567-a2f4-4dde56ff4f98","300":"instance--ede3430f-b16b-58ae-be71-1d1f1a194336","330":"instance--7772f482-8ee2-569a-b600-7528c065d4e0","60":"instance--98139a98-16b0-54fe-8c77-3473c1b520cd","90":"instance--5cb9cc95-e190-5a68-985d-0a94d39299e6"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--7","properties":[["name","Modify icons to disguise fake apps"],["description","Imitation apps for Big Sur are also created from malicious AppleScript files, in which icon files are downloaded from a C&C server, then their files are modified so that the fake app's icon is convincingly disguised as that of the legitimate app it's trying to imitate."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1036"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--5150f7cc-6f25-5eb3-a6fc-5099ced4caf4","120":"instance--64a408ce-c543-55d6-a9dd-206ce7cadbb2","150":"instance--1b71e413-cfd2-528c-8792-dc7dd1bb9938","180":"instance--aa12ce11-0165-52b6-b72d-e4d9070e9fbb","210":"instance--5d8b0f08-14bc-58f4-9316-b25a92dd09a6","240":"instance--34f96b84-9453-53f2-ae07-d28c04665e6c","270":"instance--415f1d54-1cd4-5ba7-8071-4aa99bc946ac","30":"instance--18834cac-b4c4-57b0-88ea-5a62fdb27cf9","300":"instance--de4f9957-1ac6-5782-86ea-f1a3b6a9ad13","330":"instance--8eff940b-86bb-556f-8c85-c7c47577b3ed","60":"instance--14a123fd-5626-5e69-8257-6dcd64c28ec0","90":"instance--02294ff1-7261-5db8-8e0d-b9e818922053"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--8","properties":[["name","Code sign fake apps with ad-hoc signature"],["description","But as we have seen from its source code, the malware can cleverly circumvent macOS 11's new security policies: Its fake apps and files are codesigned with an ad-hoc signature using the codesign --force --deep -s - command."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1553.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--180f2983-9c1a-56f4-99d6-c990125f7baa","120":"instance--c7f65318-7600-57f4-a8ac-992357e695ff","150":"instance--95523e1a-0a1d-52ef-944c-23f9cbc50233","180":"instance--bc8eb48d-411d-5877-aa9b-966476b71207","210":"instance--4cc5026e-07f9-5327-9912-5d278a0a3321","240":"instance--d6a7d51d-39a4-5eb3-8831-f23437781b95","270":"instance--cac30e05-5f01-5b4f-b5c0-6b975297df2d","30":"instance--cb0751b0-c027-5895-a460-a72e48920c71","300":"instance--f41cdc1f-abb7-5ff7-81c2-bf2235a7faab","330":"instance--b114cbda-9ec8-5612-b2f8-93c36811cafb","60":"instance--f28e5296-2041-5fe9-992d-4c70d549191e","90":"instance--3ea39244-da0f-5435-8745-f2afa8b13872"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--9","properties":[["name","Download pre-signed open tool"],["description","The malware then downloads its own open tool from its C&C server that comes pre-signed with an ad-hoc signature, whereas if it were on macOS versions 10.15 and lower, it would still use the system's built-in open command to run the apps."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1105"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--db5fab04-54d4-5eec-a429-185861eb2719","120":"instance--985391bd-d017-5935-ab31-3b4b56331b02","150":"instance--092bb98d-fc30-5f69-b6b7-e3024f3ec65a","180":"instance--755129e6-612e-5b63-a780-1c886d98909b","210":"instance--431723d9-dd8c-5190-9dab-6f346173c044","240":"instance--5b9fb821-54fe-5f22-bba3-038263245910","270":"instance--3c6777cb-6430-544b-b31a-01b198524553","30":"instance--c070071b-a9a3-52fe-8956-a51744db200b","300":"instance--a9a4289c-d995-5783-9544-a8b45052eb56","330":"instance--344009cc-e024-5c68-9246-51e85e00d45c","60":"instance--86c77621-2c1d-59c3-b398-e62f4b48a3dd","90":"instance--67627b08-1913-5f3d-8318-52d3bda9c1c3"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--10","properties":[["name","Execute fake apps with open tool"],["description","The malware then downloads its own open tool from its C&C server that comes pre-signed with an ad-hoc signature, whereas if it were on macOS versions 10.15 and lower, it would still use the system's built-in open command to run the apps."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1218"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--6b7baffd-afaf-5472-9af2-a263119a77ef","120":"instance--83f38e63-e29a-53f4-99d9-927a195c453f","150":"instance--3e720145-b7a1-5bd6-8a7d-bb13519675d1","180":"instance--bdce060f-d96c-5b06-b8f4-1ab1527fd01d","210":"instance--a4feb251-e6e3-5680-a712-d59c92f73ccf","240":"instance--9a564ca6-b753-5b06-880c-b3aac25c1e73","270":"instance--76861a89-f006-5e0d-8c5b-ebdcb5e926dc","30":"instance--cf41e64d-4a4b-58d9-9962-72d278b2c489","300":"instance--ac1d6edd-482f-5f13-9348-b605afcc260c","330":"instance--ed78dfa1-f300-564f-b2cd-6c99552b9a68","60":"instance--979accb3-1b3e-5af4-9182-78392cbaf904","90":"instance--ae721c42-320e-5ea4-9c77-339a05b6e12f"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--11","properties":[["name","Add new C2 domain"],["description","Days after we released our second technical brief on this malware, a new domain named \"trendmicronano[.]com\u201d was added to its C&C server. Although it contains the keywords \"trend micro\", it has nothing to do with Trend Micro. So far, six active C&C domains share the same IP address of 94[.]130[.]27[.]189:"],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0042","technique":"T1583.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--f1e35721-7ac2-54fe-bcf6-5456d2faeaa3","120":"instance--3ff6777e-fcba-5b31-bf0f-3ddf77f6030d","150":"instance--cc6192f9-21a5-5d1a-b954-6a52d989b82d","180":"instance--62a87260-0181-5f49-bc05-733216e4d822","210":"instance--2f2d05c5-8e60-5ac2-b7af-e03027d67957","240":"instance--79c1ec18-d792-5d3d-a7bc-d94fe8b124cf","270":"instance--a035d357-e930-5d33-ab8d-d0314092d036","30":"instance--3af551b8-f6ac-5f54-9f6d-403fecdc69eb","300":"instance--298b5d2a-bf93-51e9-b052-19ce36114a5d","330":"instance--c8ea0da0-a19a-5766-b0d1-8524844a59d1","60":"instance--a204f87d-ace7-5a9e-b3d1-13202bdc5c7b","90":"instance--fff4de11-3f84-52c8-bb77-192210612a62"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--12","properties":[["name","Download and execute Mach-O binaries"],["description","Because of this, we still had to examine the payload from using proper debugging methods: First, we got a decrypted shell script from , whose main payload is downloading and executing other Mach-O binary from the C&C server (Figure 19)."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1105"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--cac05670-e90e-512c-99cc-c0adf909c3ef","120":"instance--43922820-ddd3-5742-a88d-49c20f8e3fd5","150":"instance--884271a6-8d7b-5c96-9ece-61be4126898b","180":"instance--373a94ef-653d-5c24-96f7-d0cf326d3aea","210":"instance--e58b782a-e75e-5141-bdf0-6d47dbed96bd","240":"instance--5960e46a-3307-5101-b96f-f1bae10e323d","270":"instance--a5ae1125-6ca5-54f1-b9d3-0091a0a38367","30":"instance--e7c521dd-fe09-528b-bb67-1ec53389b876","300":"instance--582e0864-cb5c-5de1-b6c0-e162ae91e8bc","330":"instance--3d5550f3-3e33-5